  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:wave_drum",
      "text": [
        "The Rootbinders' craft. The Wave Drum makes Pulse from water: a little from a pond beside it, a lot from water poured into it. It is a generator, not a spare tank.",
        "It holds **1,000 Pulse**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Two ways to feed it",
      "text": [
        "**Beside water.** Water touching any face of the drum gives **3 Pulse a second**. Drums within **8 blocks** every way, edge included, piped or not, share it, rounding down: two drums make **1 a second** each, and four make nothing.",
        "**Its own water.** Fill its internal tank with a bucket, a Spirit Cistern or a Fluid Relay, and it makes **10 a second**, drinking **100 mB a second**. Nothing crowds this tier; the water is already the price. It only drinks when it actually delivers Pulse.",
        "Rain falling on the drum doubles either tier, so a roofed drum gets no rain bonus. Ranking adds **15% Pulse a second** per rank. The bonus is rounded to a whole Pulse, so a generator making only 2 or 3 a second gains nothing from its first rank. The tank holds **4,000 mB**, and water only."
      ]
    },
